From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] video: simplefb: initialize optional rotation and stride safely

The optional rot read leaves its output untouched when the property is
missing or malformed. Default rotation to zero instead of using an
uninitialized value to select a video console driver.

Only use the optional stride when its read succeeds and its value is
nonzero; otherwise retain the video uclass automatic stride calculation.
This also avoids reading an uninitialized stride after a property error.

Local fix against U-Boot v2026.10-rc5, commit
a06e89ab05eaa2b8344d521319399333cd760ae5. Source:
https://git.u-boot-project.org/u-boot/u-boot/-/blob/a06e89ab05eaa2b8344d521319399333cd760ae5/drivers/video/simplefb.c

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/simplefb.c b/drivers/video/simplefb.c
--- a/drivers/video/simplefb.c
+++ b/drivers/video/simplefb.c
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 	int ret;
 	fdt_addr_t base;
 	fdt_size_t size;
-	u32 width, height, stride, rot;
+	u32 width, height, stride;
 	struct ofnode_phandle_args args;
 
 	ret = dev_read_phandle_with_args(dev, "memory-region", NULL, 0, 0, &args);
@@ -62,14 +62,13 @@
 		log_err("%s: invalid width or height: %d\n", __func__, ret);
 		return ret ?: -EINVAL;
 	}
-	ofnode_read_u32(node, "rot", &rot);
-	uc_priv->rot = rot;
+	uc_priv->rot = ofnode_read_u32_default(node, "rot", 0);
 	uc_priv->xsize = width;
 	uc_priv->ysize = height;
 
 	/* Optional - in most cases, auto-calculation works */
 	ret = ofnode_read_u32(node, "stride", &stride);
-	if (!ret || stride)
+	if (!ret && stride)
 		uc_priv->line_length = stride;
 
 	format = ofnode_read_string(node, "format");
